          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em cobordism categories
            in the original sense of
            %a{:href => "#Stong68"} Stong 1968
            abstracts basic properties of (variants of)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds+with+boundary"} manifolds with boundary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concept+with+an+attitude"} intent
            of regarding these as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordisms"} cobordisms
            between their boundary components.
          %p
            A closely related but nominally different notion are categories whose
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            are taken to be cobordisms between their boundary components.
          %p
            Beware that the use of terminology not always brings out this distinction; but these days the second meaning is more prevalent, in particular in discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+cohomology"} cobordism cohomology
            and of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+field+theory"} topological field theory
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#cobordisms_as_objects Cobordisms as objects
          %p The axiomatization below is motivated as capturing the following familiar situation:
          %p
            The category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            and the boundary operator
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial \colon D\to D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\mapsto \partial M
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
            commuting with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sums"} direct sums
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is similar to but not actually an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mi M
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_M \colon \partial M\to M
            form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            of functors
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo →
                    %mi Id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon \partial\to Id
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
            of objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            form a set, so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+small+category"} essentially small
            (svelte).
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
            %p
              A
              %strong Stong cobordism category
              is a triple
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo ,
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (D,\partial,i)
              where
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/svelte+category"} svelte category
                  (i.e. an
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+small+category"} essentially small category
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      with finite
                      = succeed "s" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
                      = succeed "s," do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
                      = succeed ")," do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} +
                  %li
                    %p
                      including an
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mn 0
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                      (also often denoted by
                      = succeed ")," do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi ∅
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mo :
                        %mi D
                        %mo →
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial:D\to D
                  is an additive (direct-sum-preserving)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %li
                %p
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mo ∂
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Id
                          %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i:\partial\to Id_D
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
                  such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi M
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial\partial M = 0
                  for all
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi M
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi D
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\in D
            %p
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Stong68"}> Stong 1968, p. 4
            \.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Note that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is
              %em not
              required to be a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subfunctor"} subfunctor
              of the identity, i.e. the components
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_M
              are not required to be
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monic
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
            %p
              Two objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              in a cobordism category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo ,
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (D,\partial,i)
              are said to be
              = succeed "," do
                %strong cobordant
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %msub
                        %mo ∼
                        %mi cob
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\sim_{cob} N
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U,V\in D
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo +
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi U
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi N
                    %mo +
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M+\partial U \cong N+\partial V
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cong
              denotes the relation of being
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %p
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              In particular, isomorphic objects are cobordant. Being cobordant is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
              and for any object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi M
                      %msub
                        %mo ∼
                        %mi cob
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial M\sim_{cob} 0
            %p
          .un_def
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Objects of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial M
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is an object in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              are said to be
              %em boundaries
              and the objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi V
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial V = 0
              are said to be
              = succeed "." do
                %em closed
          .un_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In particular, every boundary is closed. A direct sum of closed objects (resp. boundaries) is a closed object (resp. a boundary). If an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is a boundary and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\cong N
              then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              is also a boundary.
          .un_def
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              By the above, the relation of being cobordant is compatible with the direct sum, in the sense that the direct sum induces an associative commutative operation on the set of equivalence classes, which hence becomes a commutative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              called the
              %strong cobordism semigroup
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo ,
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega(D,\partial,i)
                    \\,,
            %p
              of the cobordism category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi D
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ∂
                      %mo ,
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (D,\partial,i)
          %h3#cobordisms_as_morphisms Cobordisms as morphisms
          %p (…)
          %p
            e.g.
            %a{:href => "#GMWT09"} GMWT09, 2.1
          %p (…)
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p The following properties concern the notion ob cobordism categories with cobordisms serving as morphisms.
          %h3#GMTWTheorem The homotopy type of the cobordism category
          %h4#topological_case Topological case
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Galatius-Madsen-Tillmann-Weiss theorem)
              The loop space of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
              of the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+category"} cobordism category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cob
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cob_k
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weakly homotopy equivalent
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+loop+space"} infinite loop space
              of the spectrum
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MTO%28k%29"} MTO(k)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi N
                    %msub
                      %mi Cob
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi MTO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %mn ∞
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %mi Th
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi γ
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mrow
                              %mi k
                              %mo ,
                              %mi n
                        %mo ⊥
                      %mo )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega|N Cob_k|
                    \\simeq\Omega^\infty MTO(k)
                    \\coloneqq\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty}\Omega^{n+k}Th\left({\gamma_\mathbb{R}^{k,n}}^\perp\right).
            %p
              (Alternatively it is written as
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %msub
                        %mi Cob
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo ≃
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mi MTO
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      |N
                      Cob_k|\simeq\Omega^{\infty-1}MTO(k)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi γ
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo ,
                            %mi n
                      %mo ⊥
                    %mo ↠
                    %msub
                      %mi Gr
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\gamma_\mathbb{R}^{k,n}}^\perp\twoheadrightarrow Gr_k(\mathbb{R}^{n+k})
              is the orthogonal complement of the real
              = succeed "." do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  tautologial bundle
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/tautologial+bundle"} ?
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Galatius-Madsen-Tillmann-Weiss theorem)
              The loop space of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
              of the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oriented"} oriented
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+category"} cobordism category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Cob
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cob_k^+
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weakly homotopy equivalent
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+loop+space"} infinite loop space
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MTSO%28k%29"} MTSO(k)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi N
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Cob
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi MTSO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %mn ∞
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %mi Th
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mover
                              %mi γ
                              %mo ˜
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mrow
                              %mi k
                              %mo ,
                              %mi n
                        %mo ⊥
                      %mo )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega|N Cob_k^+|
                    \\simeq\Omega^\infty MTSO(k)
                    \\coloneqq\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty}\Omega^{n+k}Th\left({\widetilde\gamma_\mathbb{R}^{k,n}}^\perp\right).
            %p
              (Alternatively it is written as
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Cob
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo ≃
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mi MTSO
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |N Cob_k^+|\simeq\Omega^{\infty-1}MTSO(k)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mover
                            %mi γ
                            %mo ˜
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo ,
                            %mi n
                      %mo ⊥
                    %mo ↠
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi Gr
                        %mo ˜
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\widetilde\gamma_\mathbb{R}^{k,n}}^\perp\twoheadrightarrow\widetilde{Gr}_k(\mathbb{R}^{n+k})
              is the orthogonal complement of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oriented"} oriented
              real
              = succeed "." do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  tautologial bundle
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/tautologial+bundle"} ?
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#GMWT09"} Galatius, Tillmann, Madsen &amp; Weiss 2009, main theorem
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              This statement may be thought of as a limiting case, of the
              = succeed "-theorem." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
          %h4#geometric_case Geometric case
          %ul
            %li
              (
              %a{:href => "#Ayala"}> Ayala
              )
          %p
            The
            %span.newWikiWord
              Thom group
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Thom+group"} ?
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒩
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}_*
            of cobordism classes of unoriented compact smooth manifolds is the cobordism semigroup for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Diff
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=Diff_c
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %p
            Examples of cobordism categories besides those of manifolds with
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28B%2Cf%29-structure"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B,f)
                \-structure
          %ul
            %li
              “foams” used in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/link+homology"} link homology
              following
              %a{:href => "Khovanov+homology#Khovanov04"} Khovanov 2004
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/q/59677/381"} MO:q/59677
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"}> cobordism
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+cobordism"} extended cobordism
            %li
              %p
                %strong category of cobordisms
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+ring"} cobordism ring
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category+of+cobordisms"} (∞,n)-category of cobordisms
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+cobordism+category"} conformal cobordism category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+cohomology+theory"} cobordism cohomology theory
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            The notion of
            %em cobordism categories
            with cobordisms as objects is due to
          %ul
            %li#Stong68
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Stong"}> Robert Stong
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Notes on cobordism theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://pi.math.virginia.edu/StongConf/Stongbookcontents.pdf"} toc pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://press.princeton.edu/titles/6465.html"} ISBN:9780691649016
          %p
            Most authors these days use “cobordism category” to refer to the notion where cobordisms form the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
          %p
            The
            %a{:href => "#GMTWTheorem"} GMTW theorem
            about the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of the cobordisms category with topological structures on the cobordisms appears in
          %ul
            %li#GMWT09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S%C3%B8ren+Galatius"}> Søren Galatius
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ib+Madsen"} Ib Madsen
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrike+Tillmann"} Ulrike Tillmann
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Weiss"} Michael Weiss
              = succeed "," do
                %em The homotopy type of the cobordism category
              %strong 202
              2 (2009) 195–239 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0605249"}> arXiv:math/0605249
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p A generalization to geometric structure on the cobordisms is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Ayala
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Ayala"}> David Ayala
              ,
              %em Geometric cobordism categories
              thesis (2009) (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0811.2280"}> arXiv:0811.2280
              )
          %h3#embedded_cobordism_category Embedded cobordism category
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oscar+Randal-Williams"}> Oscar Randal-Williams
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Embedded Cobordism Categories and Spaces of Manifolds
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0912.2505"} arXiv:0912.2505
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedded+cobordism+category"} embedded cobordism category
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcel+B%C3%B6kstedt"}> Marcel Bökstedt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anne+Marie+Svane"} Anne Marie Svane
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A geometric interpretation of the homotopy groups of the cobordism category
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1208.3370"} arXiv:1208.3370
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcel+B%C3%B6kstedt"}> Marcel Bökstedt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Johan+Dupont"} Johan Dupont
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anne+Marie+Svane"} Anne Marie Svane
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cobordism obstructions to independent vector fields
                = succeed ")" do
